From 608439e011648c9f7b8d5b37cbf41754ec3479b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Sagvekar <sahilsagvekar230@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:38:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Keep demo and test data out of live databases

- Demo seed refuses any database that holds a real operator, and any
  non-local database unless ALLOW_DEMO_SEED is set to the exact value.
- Tests can only connect to the local freight_test database.
- provisionTenant no longer adds placeholder prices by default and no longer
  needs a password: the owner gets a random unknown one and chooses their own
  through a signed one-time link (fingerprint of the password hash makes it
  single use, no extra table).
- New `npm run tenant:create` to create a real operator and print that link.
- Add .env.example (and un-ignore it), `npm run test:unit` for DB-free tests,
  README "Going live" section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
